+# Apply instructions
+
+## Recommended complete-project method
+
+1. Back up the existing GitHub repository and production database.
+2. Extract the checkpoint ZIP.
+3. Open the extracted `limitless-ai-website` folder.
+4. Copy its contents into the existing repository root. `package.json` must be
+   at the repository root.
+5. Preserve the existing Vercel project and public domain so old browser data
+   remains on the same origin.
+6. Review `handoff/CHANGED_FILES.json` and `handoff/DELETED_FILES.json`.
+7. Install and verify with:
+
+   ```bash
+   bash handoff/verify-checkpoint.sh --install
+   ```
+
+8. Follow the Supabase and Vercel instructions in `README.md`.
+9. Commit and push with the repository owner's normal workflow.
+10. Redeploy the existing Vercel project only after the variables and migration
+    are ready.
+
+## Controlled overlay helper
+
+For an existing v5 checkout, the helper can apply only the changed paths and
+the intentional deletion. It refuses an unrelated target, refuses broad root
+targets, performs no action without `--apply`, requires explicit deletion
+consent, and backs up overwritten/deleted files beside the target repository.
+
+Preview the operation:
+
+```bash
+node handoff/apply-checkpoint.mjs /absolute/path/to/existing-repository
+```
+
+Apply it:
+
+```bash
+node handoff/apply-checkpoint.mjs /absolute/path/to/existing-repository \
+  --apply --confirm-deletions
+```
+
+The only intentional deletion from the v5 baseline is the obsolete public
+source-archive generator listed in `handoff/DELETED_FILES.json`.
+
+## Supabase
+
+No SQL is applied by the helper. For a new project, run all migrations in
+filename order. For an existing v5 project, review and run only:
+
+```text
+supabase/migrations/20260726010000_limitless_v2_atomic_sync.sql
+```
+
+Cloud writes fail closed until this additive migration is present.
+
+## Environment variables
+
+Required for sync:
+
+```dotenv
+NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
+NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_your_key
+```
+
+Optional budgeted Pollinations route:
+
+```dotenv
+NEXT_PUBLIC_POLLINATIONS_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_your_publishable_app_key
+NEXT_PUBLIC_POLLINATIONS_RUN_BUDGET=10
+```
+
+Never add an OpenRouter key, Supabase service-role key, or Pollinations `sk_`
+key to GitHub or a public environment variable.
